{"id": "EUVD-2026-85665", "enisaUuid": "b9a0aba9-ba2e-38a3-8926-4d1b1a52269f", "description": "A flaw was found in openshift/console. An unauthenticated remote attacker can exploit a misconfiguration in the CatalogdHandler, which lacks proper authentication, and the forwarding of the `openshift-session-token` cookie. This allows the attacker to send requests to the in-cluster catalogd service, leading to the disclosure of the internal operator-catalog index and providing a relay into the openshift-catalogd namespace.", "datePublished": "2026-09-23T20:48:13", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-01T16:35:24", "baseScore": 7.2, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:C/C:L/I:L/A:N", "references": ["https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:70587", "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:70617", "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:71447", "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:71450", "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:71453", "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:71454", "https://access.redhat.com/security/cve/CVE-2026-75886", "https://bugzilla.redhat.com/show_bug.cgi?id=2517886"], "aliases": ["GHSA-f8rq-4f8p-cmww", "CVE-2026-75886"], "assigner": "redhat", "epss": 0.33, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0ac8a170-8fdf-3bb7-8e56-b9cf389511cd", "product": {"name": "Red Hat OpenShift Container Platform 4.21", "vendor": {"name": "Red Hat"}}, "product_version": "patch: 1790142788"}, {"id": "51d0c556-d592-3c52-9602-5a2b80bc6dfe", "product": {"name": "Red Hat OpenShift Container Platform 4.20", "vendor": {"name": "Red Hat"}}, "product_version": "patch: 1790112153"}, {"id": "5339cb47-1a98-388a-9fdb-a5e3a30a7214", "product": {"name": "Red Hat OpenShift Container Platform 4.22", "vendor": {"name": "Red Hat"}}, "product_version": "patch: 1790130905"}, {"id": "5aab4dda-02a0-3263-bfc5-777c8329575e", "product": {"name": "Red Hat OpenShift Container Platform 4.19", "vendor": {"name": "Red Hat"}}, "product_version": "patch: 1790095950